lls it (your probe of check 3 ii). **V4 all-priority group** (`GroupSizes` without the `.Take(ShownCount(input))`) -> expect RED where a group is larger than the shown slice (the exec-16 worst case: 6 vs 4); say which row. **V5 kind guard off** (`input.Kind != NarrativeKinds.ExecutiveSummary ? [] :` -> `false ? [] :`) -> `A_group_size_is_grounded_for_the_executive_summary_only` RED. **V6 count of one** (`Where(g => g.Count > 1)` -> `>= 1`): equivalence probe: state whether any row can tell (1 is almost always grounded already: build the input where it is not, or class equivalent with the probe). **V7 risk-accepted grouped** (drop `if (f.State == DispositionStates.RiskAccepted) { paragraphs.Add([f]); continue; }`) -> the risk-accepted row RED, and (new) the validator still agrees with the provider (the shared function: run the family and say 0 `ungrounded-number`: the guard follows the grouping, which is the point). **V8 bucket dropped from the key** (m187a) -> the two-bucket row RED. **V9 first member's severity** (m187c) -> the mixed-severity row RED. **V10 first member's id only** (m187d) -> RED rows. **V11 `LeadingParagraphs` 2 -> 3** (the B66 cap arithmetic moved out of the provider; the original used `list.Count`, which is 2 at that point: prove it equals 2 at base by reading the base `Providers.cs` `:60-:76`) -> the worst-case and cap rows RED. **V12 the highest severity as MaxBy** (`MinBy(ReportVocabulary.SeverityRank)` -> `MaxBy`) -> RED (read `SeverityRank` first: lower rank = stronger, or the reverse; say which). For V0 to V12 print: red by name at head; and, where the mutation can be applied at BASE (V8, V9, V10 cannot: they do not exist there), skip; the rest is head-only. Say how many of the builder's five mutants (m187a to m187e) you reproduced with the same red counts (or the different number).
